**** end user architecture code
.ends

* DUT -- design/netlist/bandgap_amp.spice, verbatim, EXCEPT the output
* devices (MP4 drain, MN3 drain) are tied to fb_src instead of fb/out (see
* "loop-break method" above). in_p <- sns2 (non-inverting), in_n <- sns1
* (inverting) -- unchanged from design/bandgap_amp.sch's own polarity.
XMTAIL tail fb_src vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP1 d1 sns2 tail vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=20u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP2 d2 sns1 tail vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=20u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP3 pn pn vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP4 fb_src pn vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN1 d1 d1 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN2 d2 d2 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN3 fb_src d1 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN4 pn d2 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1

* DUT -- design/netlist/bandgap_startup.spice, verbatim, EXCEPT XMKFB's
* drain is tied to fb_load instead of fb (via the same 0V Vmkfb ammeter
* fixture sim/closed-loop-startup/ uses). At the settled bias this .nodeset
* seeds, XMKFB is fully released (same as every PASS point in
* sim/closed-loop-startup) and contributes ~0 current either way.
XRPU vdd det sub! rhigh w=1u l=1411.3u m=1 b=0
XMSENSE det sns1 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1
Vmkfb fb_load fbx dc 0
XMKFB fbx det vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=2u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1

* LOOP BREAK -- see "loop-break method" above. Lbreak's DC impedance is
* always 0 (ideal inductor), so it does not perturb the .nodeset-seeded DC
* operating point at all; only its AC (jwL) reactance matters, and that is
* confirmed >> this circuit's own node impedances at every frequency this
* testbench sweeps (empirically verified L-invariant between 1e6 H and
* 1e9 H during dev-time prototyping -- see README).
Lbreak fb_src brk 1e9
Vtest brk fb_load dc 0 ac 1 0


* ------------------------------------------- OP PROBE FIXTURE (issue #271)
* The bench's "op landed near its seed" check reads the DC operating point
* with `op` + `print`. Through `klt sim` that is not expressible: one
* analysis per request (AC here), measurements are `.meas` cards only (the
* batch runner's klt 0.5.0 predates `measurements[].expr`), and `.MEASURE`
* has no `op` type. So the DC bias is carried through the AC run instead:
* `acs` is an isolated node driven by its own 1 V AC / 0 V DC source, and each
* B-source below outputs V(node)*V(acs). Linearized about the operating
* point, its AC response is V(node)_dc * 1 + V(acs)_dc * v_ac(node) =
* V(node)_dc exactly (V(acs)_dc = 0), flat in frequency, real-valued. The
* B-sources only SENSE their controlling node (infinite input impedance) and
* drive nothing but their own 1 MOhm load, so the DUT is not perturbed; and
* `acs` reaches nothing but these B-sources, so Vacs adds no excitation to
* the loop Vtest measures.
Vacs acs 0 dc 0 ac 1
Bop_fb op_fb 0 V = V(fb_load)*V(acs)
Rop_fb op_fb 0 1e6
Bop_sns1 op_sns1 0 V = V(sns1)*V(acs)
Rop_sns1 op_sns1 0 1e6
Bop_sns2 op_sns2 0 V = V(sns2)*V(acs)
Rop_sns2 op_sns2 0 1e6
Bop_vref op_vref 0 V = V(vref)*V(acs)
Rop_vref op_vref 0 1e6

* Rawfile contents: the two loop-break nodes (T = V(fb_src)/V(fb_load)) and
* the four op probes. Nothing else is read, and a full `save all` rawfile at
* the fine grid would be ~100x larger.
.save v(fb_src) v(fb_load) v(op_fb) v(op_sns1) v(op_sns2) v(op_vref)

* OSDI preload only -- klt sim appends its own .control (alter + analysis).
.control
pre_osdi ${PDK_ROOT}/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi ${PDK_ROOT}/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi ${PDK_ROOT}/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi ${PDK_ROOT}/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/r3_cmc.osdi
.endc
* --- end body.spice ---
.temp -40.0
.meas ac fb_op_v find v(op_fb) at=1
.meas ac sns1_op_v find v(op_sns1) at=1
.meas ac sns2_op_v find v(op_sns2) at=1
.meas ac vref_op_v find v(op_vref) at=1
.meas ac fb_src_db_1hz find vdb(fb_src) at=1
.meas ac fb_load_db_1hz find vdb(fb_load) at=1
.control
alter r.xxtrim.rs0=1000000000000.0
alter r.xxtrim.rs1=1000000000000.0
alter r.xxtrim.rs2=1000000000000.0
alter r.xxtrim.rs3=1000000000000.0
alter r.xxtrim.rs4=1000000000000.0
alter r.xxtrim.rs5=1000000000000.0
alter r.xxtrim.rs6=1000000000000.0
alter r.xxtrim.rs7=1000000000000.0
set filetype=ascii
ac dec 30 1 1e9
write waveform.raw
quit
.endc
.end
